# tools/k/key_trade_witness.rish -- a key built to carry locality, read against the digest that
# avalanches, on one population and with one set of readings.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. active-designing/20260915-181000_the-key-that-carries-locality.md priced the
# crudest locality-bearing key there is -- a file's leading two bytes -- against the SHA3-512
# digest, and found locality, evenness and confidentiality moving as one quantity read three ways.
# That page names its own next step in its own last section: "whether a similarity-preserving
# sketch lands better on the same trade. It will land better in magnitude. Whether it CHANGES A
# SIGN is a different key, a different reading." This rung takes that step twice -- it builds the
# sketch the page named, and a third key the page never proposed. The sketch lands as forecast,
# better in magnitude and the same sign. The third key changes a sign.
#
# THE THREE KEYS, each a 16-bit value whose high byte is x and whose low byte is y, so no key gets
# a fold of its own:
#
#   sha3    -- bytes 0 and 1 of SHA3-512 over the file's bytes. The name a Tablecloth on this pier
#              would actually carry. Built to avalanche.
#   path    -- FNV-1a over the DIRECTORY in the high byte, FNV-1a over the BASENAME in the low.
#              Two files of one room share their x coordinate exactly, by construction.
#   simhash -- a 16-bit SimHash over the file's word tokens: each token's FNV-1a votes each of 16
#              accumulators up or down, and the signs are the key. Two documents sharing most of
#              their tokens agree on most signs.
#
# THREE METRICS, because a key read only in the torus's metric reports a fact about the FOLD as
# though it were a fact about the KEY: toroidal Manhattan on (x, y) with closed form 128, circular
# distance on the whole 16-bit key with closed form 16384, and Hamming distance with closed form 8.
# All three derivations are proven against a planted uniform population by the control.
#
# AND EACH RELATED POPULATION IS READ TWICE -- against the closed form, which asks whether the key
# is uniform, and against the KEY'S OWN random baseline, which asks whether the key carries the
# relation. Only the second is what locality means, and the difference is not academic: the path
# key's random pairs read a torus mean near 95 where a uniform key reads 128, so a same-directory
# mean under 128 would count that key's global concentration as though it were locality. The
# adjacency verdict takes the own-baseline reading, and the control proves the two disagree on a
# planted population that is concentrated and unrelated.
#
# WHAT IS GATED HERE, and what is only reported. The control is gated whole, and so is the live
# reading's SHAPE -- that every key answered, that no population went unread, and that the verdict
# is one of the three the scan can print. The live VERDICT is reported rather than gated, for the
# reason its sibling gives one room over: a p=0.001 test taken eighteen times refuses about one run
# in fifty-five on keys that are behaving correctly, and a gate that reds at its own stated error
# rate is a gate somebody turns off. The path key's evenness reading in particular sits near its
# critical value and is FREE -- it moves with the shape of this tree's directories.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, by tools/fixtures/k/key_trade_control.sh -- 42 behaviors on planted
# key populations and on a real directory tree in a throwaway pen:
#
#   THE ROOM-RECOVERY READING is carried over from the elder page unchanged, so the two papers may
#     be set side by side on the one property the sign change leaves untouched.
#   ALL THREE VERDICTS ARE REACHABLE from planted populations -- both_available, trade_holds, and
#     no_locality -- so the live verdict is a reading rather than a constant.
#   THE THREE CLOSED FORMS are checked against a planted uniform population in both directions:
#     the measured mean lands in its named band, AND the scan calls it indistinguishable.
#   THE CONTRAST READING is shown catching a false positive: a concentrated, unrelated population
#     reads NEARER against the closed form and flat against its own baseline, and the adjacency
#     verdict follows the second.
#   THE HASHING PATH is run on a real pen tree, since a control that only ever plants keys never
#     runs the three key functions it exists to check.
#   FOUR MUTATIONS, each bitten: the adjacency verdict read off the closed form, the torus wrap
#     dropped, the evenness grid fixed coarse, and the FNV multiply taken whole rather than split.
#   AND A SHAM LEG beneath them, because the mutants live under this tree's own root. A first draft
#     copied them to the system temporary directory, where the scan's root walk fails before it
#     reads a flag -- so all four "bites" were that walk failing. An unmutated copy in the same
#     room must still answer, or a bite there says nothing.
#
# WHAT IT LEAVES TO OTHERS. Whether Tablecloth SHOULD change its key, which is a custody-weight
# decision about a content-addressed store. Whether a key that leaks similarity leaks content,
# which is a security reading and wants its own lap. And the real store, which this never opens.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md
# Paper: active-designing/20260916-051607_the-trade-that-was-not-a-law.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/k/key_trade_witness.rish

say "key-trade: Language EN -- a key is read in its own metric before it is read in the fold's."
say "key-trade: Style Gauge, Meter -- every figure names its population, its metric, and its baseline."
say "key-trade: Lens TAME -- bound the sample, derive the closed form, prove each verdict reachable."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/k/key_trade_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "key-trade: the control must complete -- its own lines are printed above"

# All three verdicts reachable, so the live verdict is a reading rather than a constant.
assert control.out contains "leg mixed_verdict expected=verdict=both_available got=verdict=both_available ok" else "key-trade: an even and adjacent key must reach both_available"
assert control.out contains "leg lumpy_verdict expected=verdict=trade_holds got=verdict=trade_holds ok" else "key-trade: an adjacent but uneven key must reach trade_holds"
assert control.out contains "leg flat_verdict expected=verdict=no_locality got=verdict=no_locality ok" else "key-trade: a population carrying no relation must reach no_locality"
assert control.out contains "leg conc_verdict expected=verdict=no_locality got=verdict=no_locality ok" else "key-trade: a concentrated unrelated population carries no locality"

# The three columns of the mixed population, each read on its own.
assert control.out contains "leg col1_adjacent expected=no got=no ok" else "key-trade: an avalanching column must carry no adjacency"
assert control.out contains "leg col2_adjacent expected=yes got=yes ok" else "key-trade: a uniform related column must read adjacent"
assert control.out contains "leg col3_adjacent expected=yes got=yes ok" else "key-trade: a clustered related column must read adjacent"
assert control.out contains "leg col3_uneven expected=no got=no ok" else "key-trade: a clustered column must read uneven"

# The three closed forms, each proven from both directions.
assert control.out contains "leg closed_form_torus band=" else "key-trade: the torus closed form of 128 must be measured on a uniform population"
assert control.out contains "leg closed_form_ring band=" else "key-trade: the ring closed form of 16384 must be measured"
assert control.out contains "leg closed_form_hamming band=" else "key-trade: the Hamming closed form of 8 must be measured"
assert control.out contains "leg closed_form_torus_verdict expected=indistinguishable got=indistinguishable ok" else "key-trade: a uniform population must read indistinguishable from its closed form"
assert control.out contains "leg closed_form_ring_verdict expected=indistinguishable got=indistinguishable ok" else "key-trade: the ring derivation must be confirmed by the reading that uses it"
assert control.out contains "leg closed_form_hamming_verdict expected=indistinguishable got=indistinguishable ok" else "key-trade: the Hamming derivation must be confirmed by the reading that uses it"

# The contrast reading, shown catching the false positive it exists for.
assert control.out contains "leg conc_closed_form_says_nearer expected=distinguishable got=distinguishable ok" else "key-trade: the closed-form reading must call a concentrated population nearer"
assert control.out contains "leg conc_contrast_says_no expected=indistinguishable got=indistinguishable ok" else "key-trade: the own-baseline reading must refuse what the closed form admitted"
assert control.out contains "leg conc_not_adjacent expected=no got=no ok" else "key-trade: the adjacency verdict must follow the own-baseline reading"

# The hashing path, on a real pen tree rather than through the keys door.
assert control.out contains "leg tree_read expected=24 got=24 ok" else "key-trade: the real hashing path must read the pen tree"
assert control.out contains "leg tree_path_adjacent expected=yes got=yes ok" else "key-trade: the path key must carry the room relation on real files"
assert control.out contains "leg tree_sha3_onebit_hamming expected=indistinguishable got=indistinguishable ok" else "key-trade: the digest must avalanche over a one-byte edit"
assert control.out contains "leg tree_simhash_onebit_real expected=distinguishable got=distinguishable ok" else "key-trade: the SimHash must hold a one-byte edit near"

# The mutations, and the sham that makes a bite mean something.
assert control.out contains "leg mutant_room_carries_the_scan expected=verdict=both_available got=verdict=both_available ok" else "key-trade: an unmutated copy in the mutant room must still answer, or no bite can be believed"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_closed_form_adjacency expected=bite got=bite ok" else "key-trade: reading adjacency off the closed form must change a verdict"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_torus_wrap_dropped expected=bite got=bite ok" else "key-trade: the torus wrap must be load-bearing"
assert control.out contains "leg subcell_uneven_at_eight expected=no got=no ok" else "key-trade: the adaptive grid must see a cluster a coarse grid cannot"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_fixed_coarse_grid expected=bite got=bite ok" else "key-trade: the adaptive grid must be load-bearing"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_fnv_overflow expected=bite got=bite" else "key-trade: the split FNV multiply must be load-bearing"

assert control.out contains "legs=42 failures=0" else "key-trade: the control counts its own legs, so a shrunken pen cannot read as a full one"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "key-trade: the control must balance before it is believed"

# The live reading, on this tree's own bytes. Its SHAPE is gated; its verdict is reported.
let live = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/k/key_trade_scan.sh"]
say live.out
assert live.ok else "key-trade: the live reading must run on this tree, whatever it answers"
assert live.out contains "instrument=key_trade" else "key-trade: the reading names its own instrument"
assert live.out contains "population=git_ls_files" else "key-trade: the live population is the tree's own tracked bytes"
assert live.out contains "expected torus=128 ring=16384 hamming=8" else "key-trade: the three closed forms are published beside the means they judge"
assert live.out contains "rooms distinct_directories=" else "key-trade: the shape of the path key is the shape of the directory population, so it is named"
assert live.out contains "key sha3 " else "key-trade: the digest key must answer"
assert live.out contains "key path " else "key-trade: the path key must answer"
assert live.out contains "key simhash " else "key-trade: the SimHash key must answer"
assert live.out contains "contrast sha3 samedir torus " else "key-trade: every related population is read against its own baseline"
assert live.out contains "contrast path onebit hamming " else "key-trade: every key is read in every metric on every population"
assert live.out contains "contrast simhash onebit hamming " else "key-trade: the SimHash must be read in its own metric"
assert live.out contains "keys_read=3 " else "key-trade: all three keys must reach the tally"
assert live.out contains "unread_populations=0" else "key-trade: a population that went unread makes the verdict speak for less than it appears to"
assert live.out contains "critical=103.51" else "key-trade: the critical value is published beside the statistic it judges"

say "GREEN: key-trade -- 42 behaviors, all three verdicts reachable from planted populations, three closed forms matched by measurement, four mutations bitten under a sham that proves a bite is a bite, and the elder trade shown to rest on how many groups a key induces rather than on the definition of a locality key."
